[11.905, "o", "=== Argo CD cluster: helm releases in ticketflow ===\r\nNAME\tNAMESPACE\tREVISION\tUPDATED\tSTATUS\tCHART\tAPP VERSION\r\n  helm release secrets: 0\r\n\r\n=== Flux cluster: helm releases in ticketflow ===\r\nNAME      \tNAMESPACE \tREVISION\tUPDATED                                \tSTATUS  \tCHART                          \tAPP VERSION\r\nticketflow\tticketflow\t5       \t2026-09-16 09:49:37.919748855 +0000 UTC\tdeployed\tticketflow-0.1.0+2cb8a01c62ab.2\t0.1.0      \r\n  helm release secrets: 5\r\n\r\nSame chart, same commit, same application. Flux went through helm-controller\r\nand left a release you can 'helm history' and 'helm rollback'. Argo CD rendered\r\nthe chart with 'helm template' and applied it itself, so there is nothing for\r\nHelm to roll back -- undo goes through 'argocd app rollback' over Git history.\r\n"]
[16.705, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.705, "o", "\u001b[36m# Flux ran a real helm upgrade, so a release exists -- with history.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
